### Pipeline

![QueryResultImpl reads the LocalQueryEngine, which owns a WorkingSetView per database and the RegistryView, takes verdicts from merge-plan, and reads RemoteQuerySources; IndexQuerySource implements RemoteQuerySource over QueryService to the host's QueryExecutor, which compiles SQL and answers from the object snapshot index.](diagrams/pipeline.dx.svg)

```diagram
diagram flow=down
group client "@dxos/echo-client" {
  node Result "QueryResultImpl" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/query-result.ts"
  node Engine "LocalQueryEngine" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/local-query-engine.ts"
  node WorkingSet "WorkingSetView" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/working-set-view.ts"
  node Registry "RegistryView" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/registry-view.ts"
  node Plan "merge-plan" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/merge-plan.ts"
  node Remote "RemoteQuerySource" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/remote-query-source.ts"
  node Index "IndexQuerySource" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/client/index-query-source-provider.ts"
}
group host "@dxos/echo-host" {
  node Service "QueryServiceImpl" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/db-host/query-service.ts"
  node Executor "QueryExecutor" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/query/query-executor.ts"
  node Sql "SqlPlanCompiler" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/query/sql/compile.ts"
}
group core "@dxos/index-core" {
  node Snapshots "ObjectSnapshotIndex" ref="packages/core/echo/index-core/src/indexes/object-snapshot-index.ts"
}
edge Result -> Engine
edge Engine owns WorkingSet
edge Engine owns Registry
edge Engine -> Plan "verdicts"
edge Engine -> Remote
edge Index implements Remote
edge Index -> Service "QueryService"
edge Service -> Executor
edge Executor -> Sql
edge Executor -> Snapshots "index copies"
```

### Remote entry verdicts

![A remote entry for a feed item is checked against the local feed write; a flat-query entry is verified when held at its version, and otherwise its filter is re-checked; a traversal entry has its paths checked. Each check ends in verified, drop or trusted.](diagrams/verdicts.dx.svg)

```diagram
diagram flow=right
node Entry "remote entry" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/merge-plan.ts"
node Paths "check paths" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/path-revalidation.ts"
node Version "held at version?" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/merge-plan.ts"
node Filter "re-check filter" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/merge-plan.ts"
node Tail "feed local write" ref="packages/core/echo/echo-client/src/query/working-set-view.ts"
node Verified "verified"
node Drop "drop"
node Trusted "trusted"
edge Entry -> Paths "traversal"
edge Entry -> Version "flat query"
edge Entry -> Tail "feed item"
edge Version -> Verified "equal heads"
edge Version -> Filter "differ"
edge Filter -> Verified "matches"
edge Filter -> Drop "no match"
edge Filter -> Trusted "not loaded"
edge Paths -> Verified "a path holds"
edge Paths -> Drop "all broken"
edge Paths -> Trusted "unknown"
edge Tail -> Verified "matches"
edge Tail -> Drop "no match"
```

## Types

```mdl
type Completeness
  desc: |
    How much of the answer a live query holds right now. Reading it never notifies; subscribers hear only
    a change of ids or order [F-2.3].
  literals: complete | local-only | merged | stale | failed | pending
```

| Value        | Meaning                                                                                   |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `complete`   | Nothing outstanding.                                                                      |
| `local-only` | In-process results are shown; no remote has answered yet.                                 |
| `merged`     | Some remotes answered and some have not, or an answer withheld paths or a manifest.       |
| `stale`      | A remote answer predates a local write inside its scope; the re-run has not arrived.      |
| `failed`     | A remote source errored or timed out; `sources` names it.                                 |
| `pending`    | Nothing in-process contributes and no remote has answered.                                |

```mdl
type Version
  desc: |
    The state a remote evaluated an entry at. Compared for equality only: equal heads mean the tab holds
    exactly what the remote evaluated, so its own re-check would reproduce the verdict.
  variants:
    automerge: { documentId: string, heads: string[] }
    feed: { insertionId: number }
```

```mdl
type PathEdge
  desc: |
    One hop of a traversal the index took to reach a hit. The holder is the object whose document records
    the edge: the `from` side for a reference or a parent pointer, the `to` side for an incoming reference
    or a child, the relation for a relation endpoint.
  fields:
    from: EntityId
    to: EntityId
    kind: ref | incoming-ref | relation-source | relation-target | parent | child
    property?: string        # the reference's escaped property path
    holder: EntityId
    holderHeads?: string[]   # the holder's heads when the index read the edge
```

```mdl
type ManifestEntry
  desc: One member's share of a collapsed group's scalar aggregates.
  fields:
    id: EntityId
    version?: Version
    contribution: string     # JSON map of aggregate name to value: 1 for a count, the property for the rest
```

```mdl
type Verdict
  desc: What the engine does with one remote entry.
  literals: drop | verified | trusted
```

```mdl
type BranchCharacteristics
  desc: |
    The static classification `Query.characteristics(ast)` returns per branch: one record per union
    member, with wrappers above a union applied to each member.
  fields:
    class: local-complete | local-partial | local-revalidating | remote-only | unsupported
    revalidation: entry | path | manifest | none
    selection: id | type | wildcard | text | timestamp | changes | feed-cursor | incoming-ref
    predicates: local | index
    traversal: number        # hops, child-of counting as one
    window: { order: none | natural | local-property | index, limit?: number, skip?: number }
    aggregate: none | members | scalar | index
    scope: { space: boolean, feeds: boolean, registry: none | local | remote }
```

## Services

```mdl
service LocalQueryEngine
  desc: |
    The client side of every live query. Owns one WorkingSetView per database and the RegistryView, plans
    the query once, judges each remote entry, merges, and computes completeness. One engine serves one
    QueryResultImpl.
  ops:
    update(query: QueryAST.Query) → void
    getResults() → SourceEntry[]
    run(query: QueryAST.Query) → Promise<SourceEntry[]>
    getCompleteness() → Completeness
    getSourceStates() → SourceState[]
    isSynchronous() → boolean
    hasPendingSources() → boolean
    start() → void
    stop() → void
    addDatabase(database: DatabaseImpl) → void
    addRemoteSource(source: RemoteQuerySource) → void
```

```mdl
service RemoteQuerySource
  desc: |
    An out-of-process answerer: the host index, or EDGE through the same QueryService. Implemented by
    IndexQuerySource. One instance serves one engine.
  ops:
    update(query: QueryAST.Query) → void   # sets the query and starts its reactive stream
    getResults() → SourceEntry[]           # entries of the latest integrated answer
    run(query: QueryAST.Query) → Promise<SourceEntry[]>
    isServing() → boolean
    isPending() → boolean
    isFailed() → boolean
    isTruncated() → boolean
    answers() → number                     # answers integrated, unchanged re-runs included
    open() → void
    close() → void
```

```mdl
service QueryService
  desc: |
    The streamed RPC the host and EDGE both serve (`@dxos/protocols`). Every field the engine uses for
    revalidation is optional, so an old host or EDGE yields trusted entries.
  ops:
    execQuery(request: QueryRequest) → stream QueryResponse
  fields:
    QueryResult.version?: Version
    QueryResult.paths?: PathEdge[][]
    QueryResult.manifest?: ManifestEntry[]
    QueryResponse.unchanged?: boolean      # a reactive re-run whose result matches the last one sent
    QueryResponse.truncated?: paths | manifest
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: One engine, local views, remote sources

  req F-1.1:
    when: a live query is created
    then: its QueryResultImpl reads one LocalQueryEngine, which owns a WorkingSetView per database and
          the RegistryView; neither view is a query source

  req F-1.2:
    when: the engine needs an answer from outside the tab
    then: it reads RemoteQuerySources only — the host index and EDGE, both through QueryService

  req F-1.3:
    when: the engine stops and starts again
    then: stop closes the views and the remote streams, and start re-applies the current query, so a
          restarted engine serves it again
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Local writes are synchronous

  req F-2.1:
    when: an object is added, edited or removed through this database inside the scope of a branch with
          an in-process contribution
    then: the result reflects it and subscribers are notified before the writing call returns

  req F-2.2:
    when: a subscriber writes from inside a notification
    then: that write is a separate commit with its own notification, after the first commit's
          notifications are delivered

  req F-2.3:
    when: a recompute leaves the result's ids and order unchanged
    then: no subscriber is notified; a completeness transition alone is silent

  req F-2.4:
    when: a query has no order of its own
    then: entries appear in natural order (by id), wherever each object is held
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Characteristics and completeness

  req F-3.1:
    when: Query.characteristics(ast) is called
    then: it returns one BranchCharacteristics per branch, derived from the AST alone

  req F-3.2:
    when: a text, timestamp, feed-cursor, changes or in-query node appears anywhere in a branch's filter
    then: the branch's revalidation is none and nothing is dropped locally

  req F-3.3:
    when: a live query is read
    then: completeness is computed from the plan and the remote sources' states, per [Completeness]
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Versions

  req F-4.1:
    when: a remote row is sent
    then: it carries a Version — the document's id and the heads it was read at, or the feed block's
          insertion id

  req F-4.2:
    when: the indexer stores an object's copy
    then: objectSnapshot.version records the heads the copy was read at, and objectSnapshot.heads marks a
          copy at the document's saved heads that can back the row; a row stored before the version column
          reads its version from heads

  req F-4.3:
    when: a remote entry's object is held here at exactly the entry's version
    then: the entry is verified without re-evaluating the filter
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Remote entries are revalidated

  req F-5.1:
    when: a remote entry of a flat query names an object loaded here with a body
    then: the filter and the deleted option are re-evaluated against the local document; a match is
          verified and a mismatch is dropped

  req F-5.2:
    when: a remote entry names an object not loaded here, or the branch's revalidation is none
    then: the entry is trusted and shown on the remote's word, with resolution.verified false

  req F-5.3:
    when: a remote entry is verified
    then: resolution.verified is true and resolution.version is the version the remote sent
```

```mdl
feat F-6: By-id queries

  req F-6.1:
    when: every id of a live by-id query is loaded with a body in a space the query covers
    then: the engine answers from the working set alone and no remote stream is open — neither the index
          nor EDGE

  req F-6.2:
    when: a by-id query names an id that is not loaded
    then: the remote streams open, and the ids no remote answered are loaded through their documents

  req F-6.3:
    when: run() is called on a by-id query
    then: it answers the loaded ids first, then takes the remote answer, then loads only the ids no
          remote answered
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Traversal paths

  req F-7.1:
    when: a traversal reaches a hit
    then: the hit carries one path per derivation, each a list of PathEdge; both executors produce them

  req F-7.2:
    when: the engine checks a hit's paths
    then: each edge is checked against its holder's document and each level's filter against each loaded
          object; an edge whose holder is held at holderHeads stands without a read; a path is holds,
          broken or unknown, and the hit is verified when any path holds, dropped when every path is
          broken, and trusted otherwise

  req F-7.3:
    when: a hit has more than 16 paths or a compiled row more than 512 edges
    then: the hit ships no paths and is trusted

  req F-7.4:
    when: one answer's paths exceed 256 KiB
    then: the response sets truncated: paths and completeness reads merged

  req F-7.5:
    when: a traversal sits inside a union branch or a subquery
    then: its hits ship no paths and are trusted
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Aggregate manifests

  req F-8.1:
    when: a remote collapses a group of scalar aggregates (no items aggregate)
    then: the group carries a manifest: each member's id, version and share of count, sum, min and max

  req F-8.2:
    when: the engine adjusts a group
    then: it subtracts the share of each member it holds, adds the value of each local member, and lists
          local members by evaluating the query with an items aggregate appended

  req F-8.3:
    when: a local value would narrow min or max
    then: the extreme only widens, and removing a held extreme marks the group unverified

  req F-8.4:
    when: one answer's manifests exceed 256 KiB
    then: the response sets truncated: manifest and completeness reads merged
```

```mdl
feat F-9: Local ordering and windows

  req F-9.1:
    when: a query has a property or natural order and no limit or skip
    then: the engine applies the order over the merged local and remote entries, and characteristics does
          not class it as a window

  req F-9.2:
    when: a property-ordered window has a limit and no skip
    then: loaded local matches that sort at or before the last entry of a full remote window are admitted,
          re-sorted with the host's comparator and cut to the limit; a short remote window admits every
          local match

  req F-9.3:
    when: any other window is merged
    then: local evidence can only drop entries from it, never re-page it
```

```mdl
feat F-10: Feeds

  req F-10.1:
    when: an object is appended to or edited in a feed through its handle
    then: a simple selection over that feed, or over all feeds of the space, shows it before the write
          returns, and keeps showing it after the feed service acknowledges it, so it does not vanish
          before the index catches up

  req F-10.2:
    when: a feed is first opened after a query over all feeds starts
    then: its writes join that query

  req F-10.3:
    when: a remote feed entry has a local write of the same id that no longer matches
    then: the entry is dropped

  req F-10.4:
    when: a write appends, edits or deletes feed objects
    then: only the objects it names are re-evaluated, so a turn of n appends costs O(n), not O(n²)

  req F-10.5:
    when: a feed query is a window (a limit or a skip)
    then: it is remote-only
```

```mdl
feat F-11: The host answers from index copies

  req F-11.1:
    when: the memory executor matches an object whose index copy is at the document's current heads
    then: it answers from the copy and does not load the document; it counts echo.querySnapshotHits and
          echo.queryDocumentLoads

  req F-11.2:
    when: the SQL executor answers
    then: it never loads a document

  req F-11.3:
    when: a client subscription already holds a hit's document
    then: the row ships without its JSON copy or stored changes
```

## Current limits

- EDGE's executor sends no versions, paths or manifests, so every EDGE entry is trusted.
- The working set keeps no typename map: window admission and shapes without a delta scan every loaded
  object.
- A re-run already in flight when a local write lands can clear `stale` early.

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: An add notifies once, before it returns
  given: a subscribed type query that the index has answered
  when: an object of the type is added
  then:
    - the subscriber has been notified once when db.add returns
    - the index's re-run for the add notifies nobody
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: An edit that disqualifies an object removes it at once
  given: a subscribed property query holding an object
  when: the object is edited so it no longer matches
  then:
    - it is gone from results when Obj.update returns
    - the index's later answer does not bring it back
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: An edit to an unread property notifies nobody
  given: a subscribed property query
  when: an object in the result is edited on a property the filter does not read
  then: no subscriber is notified
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: A write from a notification is its own commit
  given: a subscriber that adds an object when it is notified
  when: a matching object is added
  then: the subscriber sees two notifications, one per commit, in order
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: A traversal hit leaves when its holder drops the edge
  given: an index-backed traversal hit whose edge is held by a loaded object
  when: the holder is edited to drop the reference
  then: the hit leaves the result before the edit returns
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: A count follows a local write
  given: an index-answered count over index-backed objects
  when: a member is edited out of the group
  then: the count drops by one before the edit returns
```

```mdl
scenario T-7: A property order spans local and index entries
  given: a property-ordered query with no limit, answered by the index
  when: a local object is added that sorts between two index entries
  then: it appears between them before the add returns
```

```mdl
scenario T-8: Feed writes appear at once
  given: a property query over a feed
  when: an unacknowledged write is edited into the filter, out of it, back in, then deleted
  then: it enters, leaves, enters and leaves the result as each call returns
```

```mdl
scenario T-9: Completeness follows the sources
  given: a type query and a text query
  then:
    - the type query is local-only until the index answers, then complete
    - the text query is pending until the index answers, and stale after a local write until it
      answers again
```

```mdl
scenario T-10: A by-id query over loaded ids opens no remote stream
  given: a live by-id query whose every id is loaded with a body
  then: no remote source has been given the query
```

```mdl
scenario T-11: A by-id run loads only what the index lacks
  given: a by-id run over loaded, index-only and missing ids
  then: it returns the loaded ids at once and loads only the ids no remote answered
```

```mdl
scenario T-12: Rows ship their versions
  given: a host with an indexed object, under both executors
  when: a query matches it
  then: the row's version holds the document id and the heads its copy was read at
```

```mdl
scenario T-13: Traversal hits and groups ship their evidence
  given: a host with a reference traversal and a collapsed count, under both executors
  then:
    - the traversal hit ships the edge that reached it, with its holder
    - a re-run that reaches the same hit by another edge resends it
    - the collapsed group ships each member with its share
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The query pipeline is Query API → LocalQueryEngine, which holds the working set → RemoteQuerySource, which is the index or EDGE. SpaceQuerySource and GraphQueryContext are removed.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, LocalQueryEngine, RemoteQuerySource]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Traversal results carry the paths that derived them, and the client revalidates those paths.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Aggregates carry manifests, and ordering is applied locally.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8, F-9]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Feed queries get a local half, as phase 4 of SYNC_QUERIES.md describes.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-10]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Heads go on the wire as versions.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4, Version]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A by-id query skips the remote stream when all its ids are loaded. The instruction noted that it still opens the index stream.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-7: App startup does not load Automerge documents for most objects, because nothing mutates at startup.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-11]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6uMyS9swEy81skapjfyC
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Each remote entry is dropped, verified or trusted. Local state overrules a remote entry only when the object is loaded here with a body; an unloaded object is trusted. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5, Verdict]
  why: A loaded document already contains this tab's writes and replication merges peers into it, so the local verdict is the one the merged document will give; an unloaded object has no local evidence.
  rejected:
    - Trust the remote on concurrent heads: it shows an object the tab has just edited out of the filter.
    - Ask the remote for negative evidence (id X excluded at version V): an exclusion list on every answer, to hide objects whose visible state matches.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A version is `{documentId, heads}` for a document object and `{insertionId}` for a feed block, compared for equality only. The index stores it in a new nullable objectSnapshot.version column, and objectSnapshot.heads keeps its meaning. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4, Version]
  why: Equality is all a rule acts on — equal heads skip the re-check; a loaded object is re-checked whether it is ahead, behind or concurrent. The document id is part of the version because objects move between documents.
  rejected:
    - Redefine heads as the version: a reverted build would read the new values as backing markers.
    - Ahead, behind or concurrent comparison: no rule uses it, and it costs a wasm call per entry.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: With every id loaded, both remote streams close, the index's as well as EDGE's. A loaded document is kept current by replication, so the working set alone answers the query. Fills in [D-6].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.1]
  why: The note that the index stream still opens is read as describing the gap phase 1 left open, which this closes.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: A path edge names the holder whose document records it, with the holder's heads. A path holds, is broken or is unknown; a hit is verified when any path holds and dropped only when every path is broken. Hits are capped at 16 paths, compiled rows at 512 edges and answers at 256 KiB of paths; past a cap a hit is trusted and the answer reads merged. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7, PathEdge]
  why: The holder is not the from side for three of the six edge kinds, so the edge has to be checked against the document that records it. An unknown path keeps the hit, because an unloaded holder is no evidence against it.
  rejected:
    - Per-hop frontiers instead of paths: a broken edge cannot be attributed to the hits it led to.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: A collapsed group carries each member's id, version and share of count, sum, min and max. The client replaces held members' shares with local values; min and max only widen, and removing a held extreme marks the group unverified. Manifests share the 256 KiB answer budget. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8, ManifestEntry]
  why: A count or sum is exact after subtracting and adding shares; an extreme cannot be narrowed without the runner-up, which the manifest does not carry.
  rejected:
    - Send the top k values per group so min and max narrow too: more bytes per group for a rarer case.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: The engine applies a property or natural order without limit or skip over the merged entries, and puts unordered results in id order. A property-ordered window with a limit and no skip admits local matches that sort inside the remote window; every other window is drop-only. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9, F-2.4]
  why: Without a total order an object's position depended on which source held it, so a write that loaded an index-backed object moved it ahead of the rest. A window is a slice of a set only the remote holds, so local evidence cannot re-page it.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Feed writes made through a handle join the working set as a feed tail before the write returns, and stay in it past the feed service's acknowledgement so they do not vanish before the index catches up. Each write names the objects it appended, edited or deleted, and the tail re-checks only those. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-10]
  why: Re-checking every unacknowledged write on each append made an agent turn quadratic per live query — about 3.8 s of page CPU per turn in the perf flow's assistant stage.
  rejected:
    - Coalesce appends into one notification: a write would no longer be visible before it returns.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: The memory executor answers from an object's index copy when the copy is at the document's current heads, and loads the document otherwise; the SQL executor never loads documents. Fills in [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-11]
  why: At startup nothing has changed since indexing, so the copy and the document agree, and loading the document only repeats what the copy already holds.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: A live query reports one of six completeness values, computed from its plan and its sources. Subscribers hear only a change of ids or order, so a completeness transition alone is silent. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3, F-2.3, Completeness]
  why: Before this a failed stream looked like an empty answer and a held re-run looked complete; a UI needs to tell those apart without being re-rendered for each transition.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: Every revalidation field on the wire is optional. An old host or EDGE omits them, and the engine treats their entries as trusted. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [QueryService]
  why: The host, EDGE and clients deploy separately; optional fields keep every pairing working without a protocol version.
```
